WEBVTT

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:04.102
which becomes her offspring’s nursery—
and the cockroach’s crypt.

00:01:04.685 --> 00:01:06.229
Over the following weeks,

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:09.774
her larva hatches,
bores into the cockroach,

00:01:09.774 --> 00:01:13.277
eats it alive, pupates in its carcass,

00:01:13.277 --> 00:01:17.031
and emerges as an iridescent adult.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:23.746
This gruesome tale is just one example
of parasitoidism,

00:01:24.122 --> 00:01:28.126
an evolutionary strategy employed
by most wasps.

00:01:28.126 --> 00:01:31.838
Parasitoids feed off other animals 
as they develop,